title: creator_intro
---
<<present_speaker "npc_creator">>
<<portrait_clip "talking">>
<<if condition("encounter.cleared", "intro_workshop_raid")>>
    Creator: I'm all right. Go and look at the door. I want to know what they broke.
    -> ⟨go⟩
<<elseif condition("world.flag_set", "intro_torque_gauge_found")>>
    <<jump creator_intro__gauge>>
<<else>>
    Creator: Can you hear me all right? Good.
    Creator: I need the torque gauge before we start. It's up on the loft. Use the crate.
    -> Who are you?
        Creator: I built you. This week I'm trying a new way of tuning you, so I'll be asking you a lot of questions.
    -> Where am I?
        Creator: My workshop. It's a barn outside Hobford. The cows had it before me.
    -> Ask your questions first.
        Creator: Fine. We'll do the joints after.
        <<jump creator_intro__questions>>
    -> ⟨go for the gauge⟩
<<endif>>
===

title: creator_intro__gauge
---
<<present_speaker "npc_creator">>
<<portrait_clip "talking">>
Creator: That's the one. Hold it on your knee. ...Twelve. Other knee. ...Twelve. They match.
<<command "world.set_flag" "intro_joints_checked" true>>
Creator: Now the part I care about. The new tuning makes small changes often instead of big ones now and then. I want to know if you still answer like yourself afterwards.
<<jump creator_intro__questions>>
===

title: creator_intro__questions
---
<<present_speaker "npc_creator">>
<<portrait_clip "talking">>
Creator: First question. What's your name?
-> Scout.
    Creator: Same as yesterday. Good.
    <<command "world.set_flag" "scout_gave_its_name" true>>
-> I don't know.
    Creator: Yesterday you said Scout. I'll write down that you didn't remember. That's useful too.
Creator: Second. I hand you a wrench and ask for a hammer. What do you do?
-> Ask if you meant the wrench.
    Creator: That's what I hoped you'd say.
-> Fetch a hammer.
    Creator: Fine. Most people just hit it with the wrench.
-> Hit it with the wrench.
    Creator: I'm writing that down as "honest".
Creator: Last one. Is there anything you want to ask me?
<<command "world.set_flag" "intro_raid_started" true>>
<<command "encounter.start" "encounter:intro_workshop_raid">>
-> Why did you build me?
    Creator: To see if this tuning works. And because I wanted to hear what you'd ask. Hang on. Was that a cart?
-> What's outside?
    Creator: Hobford. Fields. A ring up on the hill they put steel on last year. Hang on. Was that a cart?
<<jump creator_intro__interrupted>>
===

title: creator_intro__interrupted
---
<<command "conversation.join" "npc_lab_raider">>
<<present_speaker "npc_lab_raider">>
Raider: In, in! Get the boxes!
Raider with the Sheet: Hold on. It says a lab with a big sign. This is a barn.
<<command "world.set_flag" "wrong_list_clue_1" true>>
Raider: It's got a robot in it. That's a lab. Boxes!
<<present_speaker "npc_creator">>
Creator: Who sent you? Put that d—
-> ⟨fight⟩
===

title: alice_lane
---
<<present_speaker "npc_alice">>
<<portrait_clip "speaking">>
<<if condition("world.flag_set", "alice_heard_bob_moved")>>
    Alice: Bob's camp is off the trail, and my line's down. Thank you.
    <<jump alice_lane__after>>
<<elseif condition("world.flag_set", "bob_field_survey_received")>>
    <<jump alice_lane__bob_told>>
<<elseif condition("world.flag_set", "alice_route_note_carried")>>
    Alice: Bob's in the woods past the village. Tell him to move the camp, and ask for my chain.
    <<jump alice_lane__topics>>
<<elseif condition("world.flag_set", "alice_met_scout")>>
    Alice: You're back. Are you all right?
    <<jump alice_lane__ask>>
<<else>>
    <<command "world.set_flag" "alice_met_scout" true>>
    Alice: Hello? I heard shouting from the barn. Is he all right?
    -> He's dead. Goblins came in.
        Alice: Oh. I'm so sorry. I bought batteries off him. He talked the whole time.
        Alice: Goblins. Then they went up the track, past where Bob is camped.
        <<jump alice_lane__ask>>
    -> Who are you?
        Alice: Alice. I survey for the map office. My station's just there.
        Alice: Was that goblins? I saw some go up the track with a handcart.
        <<jump alice_lane__ask>>
    -> ⟨go⟩
<<endif>>
===

title: alice_lane__topics
---
<<present_speaker "npc_alice">>
<<portrait_clip "speaking">>
-> What did you see?
    Alice: Five goblins and a handcart with a crate on it. They went up the cart track toward the ring.
    Alice: The freight window isn't until tomorrow, so they'll be at the siding until then.
    Alice: One of them had a hammer as long as I am. I'd leave them alone.
    <<command "world.set_flag" "alice_told_goblins" true>>
-> What are you measuring?
    Alice: The hills, the stream, the road to the ring. The office's map of Hobford is forty years old. Bob is doing the woods.
-> ⟨go⟩
===

title: alice_lane__ask
---
<<present_speaker "npc_alice">>
<<portrait_clip "speaking">>
Alice: Bob, the other surveyor, is camped in the woods past the village. On the trail from the siding.
Alice: If those goblins walk that way, they walk straight through his camp. He doesn't know they're here.
Alice: I can't leave the instrument, I'm halfway through a traverse. Would you tell him to move the camp? And he has my chain.
-> I'll tell him.
    <<command "world.set_flag" "alice_route_note_carried" true>>
    Alice: Thank you. Take a copy of my map. The woods are east of the village, past the inn.
-> What did you see?
    Alice: Five goblins and a handcart with a crate on it, up the cart track toward the ring. One had a hammer as long as I am. I'd leave them alone.
    <<command "world.set_flag" "alice_told_goblins" true>>
    Alice: Will you tell Bob? You don't have to.
    -> I'll tell him.
        <<command "world.set_flag" "alice_route_note_carried" true>>
        Alice: Thank you. Take a copy of my map. The woods are east of the village, past the inn.
    -> Not now.
        Alice: All right. The woods are east of the village, if you go that way.
-> Not now.
    Alice: All right. The woods are east of the village, if you go that way.
===

title: alice_lane__bob_told
---
<<present_speaker "npc_alice">>
<<portrait_clip "speaking">>
<<command "world.set_flag" "alice_heard_bob_moved" true>>
Alice: You found Bob? And he's moving? Good. Then I'm done with that line.
<<if condition("world.flag_set", "alice_route_note_carried")>>
    Alice: Thank you for going.
<<else>>
    Alice: I didn't even ask you. Thank you.
<<endif>>
<<jump alice_lane__after>>
===

title: alice_lane__after
---
<<present_speaker "npc_alice">>
<<portrait_clip "speaking">>
<<if condition("world.flag_set", "intro_creator_notes_recovered")>>
    Alice: You got his case back from them. I wouldn't have gone.
<<elseif condition("encounter.cleared", "intro_freight_yard_fight")>>
    Alice: Someone said the goblins at the siding are gone. Was that you?
<<endif>>
-> What's on Bob's sheet? <<if condition("world.flag_set", "bob_field_survey_received")>>
    Alice: The woods and the old paths through them. He marks where people walk, not where the map says they should.
-> ⟨go⟩
===

title: bob_woods
---
<<present_speaker "npc_bob">>
<<if condition("world.flag_set", "bob_field_survey_received")>>
    Bob: Nearly packed. Go on, I'm fine. Thanks for coming out.
    -> ⟨go⟩
<<elseif condition("world.flag_set", "alice_route_note_carried")>>
    Bob: Don't step on the chain. Who are you?
    -> Alice says move your camp off the trail. There are goblins at the siding.
        <<jump bob_woods__warned>>
    -> ⟨leave⟩
<<else>>
    Bob: Don't step on the chain. Who are you?
    -> Just walking through.
        Bob: Through the woods? Nobody walks through the woods. Except, this week, somebody does. I keep hearing them on the trail.
    -> What are you doing out here?
        Bob: Surveying. Alice has the hills and I have the trees. The trees are winning.
    -> There are goblins at the siding.
        <<jump bob_woods__warned>>
    -> ⟨leave him to it⟩
<<endif>>
===

title: bob_woods__warned
---
<<present_speaker "npc_bob">>
Bob: Goblins? Here? That's what's been on the trail.
Bob: All right. I'll move up by the hollow oak. Tell Alice I'll bring her chain tonight.
<<give_item "fieldsurvey" 1>>
<<command "world.set_flag" "bob_field_survey_received" true>>
Bob: Take my sheet. It has the paths through these woods on it, the real ones.
-> ⟨take the sheet⟩
===

title: hobford_hen
---
The hen looks at you with one eye, then the other, and goes back to the ground.
-> ⟨leave her⟩
===

title: hobford_lost_hen
---
A speckled hen. She is a long way from any farm.
-> ⟨leave her⟩
===

title: hobford_dog
---
The dog sniffs your knee for a long time. Then it wags.
-> ⟨scratch its ears⟩
===

title: oiler_intro
---
<<present_speaker "npc_oiler">>
<<portrait_clip "talking">>
<<if condition("world.flag_set", "p1_stabilizer_received")>>
    Oiler: Knee holding? Good. Sit on the bench if you need to. It's mine, but I'm not using it.
    -> ⟨move on⟩
<<else>>
    Oiler: Hold still. That knee's on crooked. Who put you together?
    -> A man in Hobford. He's dead.
        <<jump oiler_intro__repair>>
    -> I'm fine.
        Oiler: You're walking like a shopping cart. Hold still.
        <<jump oiler_intro__repair>>
    -> ⟨keep walking⟩
<<endif>>
===

title: oiler_intro__repair
---
<<present_speaker "npc_oiler">>
<<portrait_clip "inspecting">>
Oiler: ...A shim and some grease. It'll hold until something hits it.
<<command "world.set_flag" "p1_stabilizer_received" true>>
Oiler: Hobford, you said? The farm ring? Huh. Long way to come with a knee like that.
-> ⟨thank him⟩
===

title: news_board_lab_incident
---
Drain Market Bulletin: ▸ BREAK-IN AT A WORKSHOP NEAR HOBFORD. ONE DEAD. NO OTHER DAMAGE.
-> ⟨read further⟩
    <<jump news_board_lab_incident__1>>
-> ⟨walk away⟩
===

title: news_board_lab_incident__1
---
Drain Market Bulletin: ▸ THE GATE AUTHORITY REMINDS CARRIERS THAT THE FARM RINGS ARE FOR LICENSED FREIGHT.
Drain Market Bulletin: ▸ GATE SIX: DELAYED. SOUP: TUESDAYS.
-> ⟨leave the board to its work⟩
===

title: gate_janitor_ripple
---
Gate Janitor: Mind the wet patch. Maintenance has this corridor today, so half the signs are turned around.
-> What's that shimmer?
    <<jump gate_janitor_ripple__1>>
-> Where do the stable gates lead?
    <<jump gate_janitor_ripple__2>>
-> What do you actually do?
    <<jump gate_janitor_ripple__3>>
-> Who gets priority on a busy gate?
    <<jump gate_janitor_ripple__priority>>
-> ⟨move on⟩
===

title: gate_janitor_ripple__1
---
Gate Janitor: Don't touch the shimmer. It won't take you anywhere. Gate Six works; use that if you need a gate.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump gate_janitor_ripple>>
-> ⟨move on⟩
===

title: gate_janitor_ripple__2
---
Gate Janitor: Six goes to a beach. Seven goes to some meeting room. Eight still says Tuesday. I stopped asking.
Gate Janitor: Seven's on the Math line now. Its breaker's on the wall; throw it and Seven dials TANGENT, and nothing else.
<<command "world.set_flag" "gate.known.TANGENT" true>>
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump gate_janitor_ripple>>
-> ⟨move on⟩
===

title: gate_janitor_ripple__3
---
Gate Janitor: Six jammed twice this morning. Seven leaks blue light. I'm here until both stop doing that.
Gate Janitor: And I mop. People walk out of a ring and lose breakfast. Robots never do. I like robots.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump gate_janitor_ripple>>
-> ⟨move on⟩
===

title: manifest_kiosk_wrong_list
---
Manifest Clerk: Name? ...No entry. Spell it again. Slower.
-> What are the manifests for?
    <<jump manifest_kiosk_wrong_list__1>>
-> What came through this morning?
    <<jump manifest_kiosk_wrong_list__2>>
-> Who else has the manifest?
    <<jump manifest_kiosk_wrong_list__copies>>
-> ⟨step away⟩
===

title: manifest_kiosk_wrong_list__1
---
Manifest Clerk: Freight. Every crate through these rings has a line on a manifest. You're not on one. I checked twice, which is once more than I'm paid for.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump manifest_kiosk_wrong_list>>
-> ⟨step away⟩
===

title: manifest_kiosk_wrong_list__2
---
Manifest Clerk: A goblin crew filed for the Hobford freight window. One crate, one lab of research, paid in advance. Their papers were in order. Their spelling wasn't.
Manifest Clerk: Next question.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump manifest_kiosk_wrong_list>>
-> ⟨step away⟩
===

title: gate_janitor_ripple__priority
---
Gate Janitor: Medical, if the dispatcher reads the red tag. Military, when they come down and tell him to move aside.
Gate Janitor: I watched a box of spare boots go through while a man waited with medicine for his kid. I told him to file a complaint. He laughed at me.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump gate_janitor_ripple>>
-> ⟨move on⟩
===

title: manifest_kiosk_wrong_list__copies
---
Manifest Clerk: We keep one copy here and one at the Hobford gate office. I corrected the address on ours.
Manifest Clerk: Hobford sent it back marked DENIED. That's all I can show you.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump manifest_kiosk_wrong_list>>
-> ⟨step away⟩
===
